<!--
    Screen-reader names for control-template parts that ship WITHOUT one.

    A control's default template can contribute interactive elements that the markup
    hosting the control never sees, so no amount of AutomationProperties.Name in a view
    reaches them, and a static AXAML scan cannot find them either — there is no element
    in the markup to scan.  Naming them is the theme's job, which is why this file sits
    beside the theme bundle rather than in any one app.

    ── NumericUpDown / ButtonSpinner ────────────────────────────────────────────────
    NumericUpDown draws a ButtonSpinner, whose template puts two RepeatButtons
    (PART_IncreaseButton / PART_DecreaseButton) beside the text box.  Their Content is a
    PathIcon, and Avalonia's ContentControlAutomationPeer falls back to Content.ToString()
    when no name is set — so a screen reader announces each one as the literal string
    "Avalonia.Controls.PathIcon".  Measured through UIA 2026-09-07 on both apps: every
    NumericUpDown on screen contributed two such buttons (four on ClaudeForge's Essentials
    page, six on OpenCodeForge's).  The NumericUpDown itself is fine — it carries the name
    its view sets and surfaces as a correctly-named ControlType.Spinner.

    The /template/ selector is required: without it the style does not reach an element
    that lives inside a control template.  Names come from WrapperStrings so a host can
    localise them through the same Resolver hook the wrapper chrome uses; the default is
    English.

    Guard: LayeredEditors.Avalonia.Tests/Themes/SpinnerAutomationNameTests.cs applies this
    file's styles to a real templated NumericUpDown and reads the automation peers.
-->
<Styles xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
        xmlns:loc="using:Bennewitz.Ninja.LayeredEditors.Avalonia.Localization">

    <Style Selector="ButtonSpinner /template/ RepeatButton#PART_IncreaseButton">
        <Setter Property="AutomationProperties.Name"
                Value="{x:Static loc:WrapperStrings.LabelSpinnerIncrease}" />
    </Style>

    <Style Selector="ButtonSpinner /template/ RepeatButton#PART_DecreaseButton">
        <Setter Property="AutomationProperties.Name"
                Value="{x:Static loc:WrapperStrings.LabelSpinnerDecrease}" />
    </Style>

</Styles>
